<title>USA: Connecticut Democrats win control of state senate.</title>
<headline>Connecticut Democrats win control of state senate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unofficial returns showed Democrats gained control of the Connecticut Senate with at least a 19-to-17 majority.</p>
<p>This means that Republican Gov. John Rowland will be without a party majority in either the House or the Senate for the remaining two years of his term.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
